content='''<div class="p5-hide"><p>Manual draft only: no sending, signing, payment collection or legal advice. <a href="/downloads/business-proposal-template.pdf" download>Download the two-page blank proposal PDF</a>.</p><noscript><p>Editable controls need JavaScript; the PDF and guide remain available.</p></noscript><h2>Prepare your proposal</h2><form id="p5-form">'''+fields+'''<h3>Itemized pricing (USD; 1–20 lines)</h3><div id="p5-rows"></div><button id="p5-add" type="button">Add price line</button><button type="submit">Review proposal</button><button id="p5-sample" type="button">Load fictional example</button></form><p id="p5-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></div><h2>Your reviewed proposal</h2><div id="p5-result" aria-live="polite"></div><div class="p5-hide"><h2>Keep your draft</h2><p>No automatic saving or synchronization. Reloading or closing loses entries unless you keep a JSON backup. This worksheet does not transmit your entries. Avoid unnecessary personal details and keep backups private.</p><button id="p5-backup" type="button">Download editable JSON backup</button><label>Import same-tool JSON (64 KB maximum)<input id="p5-import" type="file" accept=".json,application/json"></label><button id="p5-export" type="button" disabled>Download reviewed text</button><button id="p5-print" type="button" disabled>Print / Save PDF</button><button id="p5-clear" type="button">Clear entries</button><dialog id="p5-import-dialog"><h2>Replace current entries?</h2><p>A valid backup is ready. Import replaces the entries on this page.</p><button id="p5-confirm" type="button">Replace entries</button><button id="p5-cancel" type="button">Cancel</button></dialog><dialog id="p5-clear-dialog"><h2>Clear page entries?</h2><p>Downloaded backups remain on your device.</p><button id="p5-clear-confirm" type="button">Clear entries</button><button id="p5-clear-cancel" type="button">Cancel</button></dialog><h2>How to use this proposal template</h2><p>Start with the client objective. Define deliverables, revision limits, acceptance criteria, excluded work, delivery timing and client dependencies. Record what happens when inputs or approvals are late. Enter “none” when a required section truly has no item; do not present an unknown obligation as settled.</p><p>A proposal supports one client engagement. A <a href="/journal/business-plan-guide/">business plan</a> describes the whole operation. This draft records neither agreement nor payment. Confirm appropriate commercial and legal terms for the actual work before relying on an offer.</p><h3>Price and deposit formulas</h3><p>Each line is whole quantity multiplied by USD unit price. Total adds the lines in integer cents. Proposed deposit equals total times the entered whole percentage, rounded to the nearest cent. Balance equals total minus deposit. No taxes, discounts, currency conversion or recurring billing are calculated. Confirm required additions separately before issuing a final price.</p><h3>Original fictional example</h3><p>One discovery workshop at $300, six page drafts at $150 each and one revision round at $200 total $1,400. A 30% deposit is $420, leaving $980. Design, coding and ongoing changes are excluded. Timing depends on client inputs and must be converted into confirmed dates before agreement. These are invented figures, not recommended market rates.</p><h3>Review, export and restore</h3><p>Any edit invalidates the old report and disables text export and print until reviewed again. Text export is a static draft. JSON is the editable same-tool backup. Import checks format, limits, dates and amounts and asks before replacing current entries. The separate PDF is a static two-page US Letter writing template, not fillable. Browser Print / Save PDF prints the reviewed report; inspect pagination and device options.</p><h3>Limits and next step</h3><p>Use 1–20 price lines, whole quantities 1–1,000 and unit prices $0–$1,000,000 with at most two decimals. Valid-until cannot precede issue date. No e-signatures, sending, payment records, CRM sync or automatic saving are provided. Assign the next review with the <a href="/journal/sales-automation-guide/">sales handoff guide</a>; check hours against the <a href="/journal/consulting-business-plan/">consulting capacity example</a>.</p><h3>Frequently asked questions</h3><p><strong>Can I edit the PDF?</strong> Restore JSON here for editable calculated inputs; the PDF is a writing copy.</p><p><strong>Does this record acceptance?</strong> No. Confirm agreement separately.</p><p><strong>Is the deposit a payment?</strong> No. It is a proposed amount, not money collected.</p></div>'''
